# 7. Breadth First Search (Optimal)

## 7.1 Intuition

Imagine every number as a node.

```
1

↓

12

↓

123

↓

1234
```

Every number can generate only one child.

BFS naturally generates numbers in sorted order.

---

## 7.2 Logic

Initially

```
Queue

1

2

3

...

9
```

Pop

```
12

Generate

123
```

Pop

```
45

Generate

456
```

Continue until queue becomes empty.

---

## 7.3 Algorithm

```
Push

1..9

while queue

    pop front

    if inside range

        answer

    last=num%10

    if last<9

        push

        num*10+last+1
```

---

## 7.4 Code

```python
from collections import deque

class Solution:
    def sequentialDigits(self, low: int, high: int):

        ans = []

        q = deque(range(1,10))

        while q:

            num = q.popleft()

            if num > high:
                continue

            if low <= num <= high:
                ans.append(num)

            last = num % 10

            if last < 9:
                q.append(num*10+last+1)

        return ans
```

