# 8. Depth First Search

## 8.1 Intuition

Instead of queue, recursively build numbers.

Example

```
1

↓

12

↓

123

↓

1234
```

---

## 8.2 Logic

Recursive relation

```
dfs(num)

last=num%10

dfs(num*10+last+1)
```

---

## 8.3 Algorithm

```
DFS from

1..9

Store valid numbers

Sort answer
```

---

## 8.4 Code

```python
class Solution:
    def sequentialDigits(self, low: int, high: int):

        ans=[]

        def dfs(num):

            if num>high:
                return

            if low<=num<=high:
                ans.append(num)

            last=num%10

            if last<9:
                dfs(num*10+last+1)

        for i in range(1,10):
            dfs(i)

        return sorted(ans)
```

